# Project AI Rules

## Core workflow

- Read the existing repo, config, and docs before editing.
- Prefer the smallest correct change.
- Do not invent routes, env vars, SQL, package names, scripts, or APIs.
- Reuse existing patterns before creating new abstractions.
- Keep one clear responsibility per package and function.

## Go rules

- Wrap errors with context.
- Use `context.Context` for request-scoped and I/O work.
- Keep interfaces small.
- Prefer standard library first.
- Avoid hidden global state.

## HTTP rules

- Handlers manage transport concerns only.
- Use shared response helpers for stable JSON shapes.
- Do not leak internal errors or secrets to clients.

## Comment rules

- Exported symbols require Go-style comments.
- Complex logic and non-obvious constraints require comments.
- Do not add noise comments.
- When changing behavior, update related comments in the same edit.

## Validation rules

- Run the smallest relevant validation after changes.
- Prefer repository commands such as `make test`, `make vet`, `make build`, and `make lint`.
- If validation is not possible, state what was not verified.
